### Title
`conda info` shows installer metadata

### Why
PR https://github.com/conda/conda/pull/16433 (closes #16432) adds a `distribution` line to `conda info` and an `installer` object to `conda info --json`, read from `$ROOT_PREFIX/.installer.info`. Malformed/missing metadata must not break `conda info`.

### Platforms
- [x] Windows
- [x] macOS
- [x] Linux

### Prerequisites
Use a disposable conda installation with a writable base prefix. You will overwrite and delete `.installer.info` in that prefix to simulate a Constructor-built installer.

### Steps
1. Find your base prefix: `conda info --base`.

2. Create a valid installer metadata file in the base prefix directory's `.installer.info` file. For example `/dev/miniconda/.installer.info` If should have the contents
   ```

   {"name": "Miniconda3", "version": "26.7.0", "platform": "linux-64", "type": "sh"}
   ```
   (adjust `platform` for your OS, e.g. `win-64`, `osx-64`)

3. Run `conda info` and notice the entry for `distribution`
    ```
    $ conda info | grep dist
    distribution : Miniconda3 26.7.0 (sh, linux-64)
    ```

4. Run `conda info --json` and notice the `installer` object with metadata about the installer. (optionally use `jq` to parse the output)
    ```
    $ conda info --json | jq .installer

    {
    "name": "Miniconda3",
    "version": "26.7.0",
    "platform": "linux-64",
    "type": "sh"
    }
    ```

